        "# Alien Delivery - H3 + Pika, first + last frame (sage attention)\nThe same H3 + Pika setup with a **last frame**: used where a shot must end on an exact picture with the camera locked (the chameleon changing colour on the bridge, the door scene, the reveal). Real settings and prompt of the final shot E2.\n\nThe film's frames for this shot are in `inputs/` (`alien_delivery_E2_first.png`, `alien_delivery_E2_last.png`): copy them into `ComfyUI/input` and queue. For your own shot: both frames must share the same camera and set; change only what moves, or H3 morphs between them.\n\n## Models\n- **H3 FL2VA (first/last frame + audio) base model, pruned, int8** (20.97 GB)  \n  file `minimax_h3_fl2va_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors` -> put in `ComfyUI/models/diffusion_models/`  \n  https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3/resolve/main/diffusion_models/minimax_h3_fl2va_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors\n- **Pika H3 Flex LoRA for FL2VA (6-step sampling)** (1.96 GB)  \n  file `pika_h3_flex_fl2va_comfy_bf16.safetensors` -> put in `ComfyUI/models/loras/`  \n  https://huggingface.co/Pika-Labs/Pika-H3-Flex/resolve/main/comfy/loras/pika_h3_flex_fl2va_comfy_bf16.safetensors\n- **Qwen3-VL 32B text encoder for H3, NVFP4 AWQ** (15.69 GB)  \n  file `qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_nvfp4_awq.safetensors` -> put in `ComfyUI/models/text_encoders/`  \n  https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_nvfp4_awq.safetensors\n- **H3 video VAE, int8 (Kijai's build, the one used here)** (3.17 GB)  \n  file `minimax_h3_video_vae_int8_convrot.safetensors` -> put in `ComfyUI/models/vae/`  \n  https://huggingface.co/Kijai/MiniMax-H3-experimental/resolve/main/minimax_h3_video_vae_int8_convrot.safetensors\n- **H3 audio VAE** (0.61 GB)  \n  file `minimax_h3_audio_vae_fp32.safetensors` -> put in `ComfyUI/models/vae/`  \n  https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3/resolve/main/vae/minimax_h3_audio_vae_fp32.safetensors\n\n## Custom nodes\n- **ComfyUI-KJNodes** (kijai) for *Patch Sage Attention KJ*: https://github.com/kijai/ComfyUI-KJNodes - needs SageAttention installed in ComfyUI's Python. (The int8 attention of the opening-frame workflow was not tested with first + last frame, so these shots used sage.)\n\n## Settings that matter\n- 1632x928, length 158 = 6.58 s at 24 fps; sampler `lcm` with Pika's 6-step sigmas; Basic Guider.\n- The prompt adds a second alignment line: \"At 6.00 seconds into the target video, <Picture 2> ... is fully referenced\", and keeps every character in both frames.\n\n## How the film was made\n1. **Frames** - every shot opens on a still drawn with Codex image generation (1672x941, cropped to 1632x928). One master view per scene; close shots are crops of it, re-detailed.\n2. **Shots** - this H3 + Pika workflow, 6 s each (158 frames, 24 fps), opening frame, or first + last frame where both frames share one locked camera.\n3. **Upscale** - NVIDIA RTX Video Super Resolution to 2560x1440 (NVIDIA Visual Enhancer `VE_CLI.exe`, outside ComfyUI). It must run on the 24 fps original, before smoothing.\n4. **Smoothing** - the RIFE x2 workflow, per shot (never across a cut, RIFE makes a ghost frame at hard cuts) -> 48 fps.\n5. **Music** - Google Lyria 3.5 (instrumental, \"retro sci-fi comedy space funk, 112 BPM\"), mixed ~14 LU under the dialogue with sidechain ducking in FFmpeg.\n\nMachine: RTX 3080 10 GB, 64 GB RAM, ComfyUI 0.44.0, PyTorch 2.11 + CUDA 13.0."
      ],
